.TH MU2EDAQ-OTSDAQ 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.2.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-otsdaq \- mu2edaq\-tools otsdaq: query otsdaq over xdaq HTTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-tools otsdaq
.I read\-command
.RI [ arguments ]
.RI [ connection\-options ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-watch
.RB [ \-\-interval
.IR S ]
.RB [ \-\-count
.IR N ]]
.br
.B mu2edaq\-tools otsdaq raw
.I REQUEST_TYPE
.RB [ \-\-service
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-lid
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-handler
.BR request | state\-machine ]
.RB [ \-\-query
.IR K=V ]...
.RB [ \-\-form
.IR K=V ]...
.RB [ \-\-xml ]
.RI [ connection\-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every request is an HTTP
.B POST
to
.IB origin /urn:xdaq\-application:lid= LID /Request?RequestType= NAME ,
or for
.BR "raw \-\-handler state\-machine" ,
to
.BI .../StateMachineXgiHandler?StateMachine= NAME .
The response must be XML with root
.BR ROOT ;
an
.B Error
element, an
.B error
field in
.BR DATA ,
or
.B state_transition_attempted=0
is reported as an error.
.PP
The typed read commands send only otsdaq getter request types and never a
CookieCode.
They are read-only in so far as those getters are; that is otsdaq-core
behaviour and is not verifiable from this package.
.PP
.B raw
is not read-only.
It posts any request type to any LID, including state transitions
.RB ( \-\-handler state\-machine ),
FE macro execution
.RB ( runFEMacro ,
LID 800) and configuration writes (LID 281).
It prints a warning on stderr and proceeds without confirmation.
.SS Origins
.TP
Gateway, Console, Macro Maker, Configuration
.I gateway_url
(LIDs 200, 260, 800, 281).
.TP
Slow Controls
.IR slow_controls_url ,
default the gateway port plus one (LID 282).
.TP
TFM
.IR tfm_url ,
default the gateway host on port 3047 (LID 302).
The port is a constant taken from the CRV web client, so every profile without
an explicit
.I tfm_url
on the same host, or tunnelled to
.BR localhost ,
resolves to the same TFM; set
.I tfm_url
per profile.
.PP
Origins must be
.B http
or
.B https
with no path, query, fragment or credentials.
.SH READ COMMANDS
.TP
.B state
.B getCurrentState
(LID 200).
.TP
.B run\-info \fR[\fIRUN_NUMBER\fR]
.B getRunInfo
(LID 200); 0 or omitted means the current run.
.TP
.BR daq\-report ", " daq\-state
.BR getDAQReport ,
.B getDAQState
(TFM).
.TP
.B macros
.B getFEMacroList
(LID 800): FE, public and private macros.
Lists, does not execute.
.TP
.B pv\-list
.B getList
(Slow Controls).
.TP
.BI pv\-read " PV" " \fR...\fP"
.BR getPvData .
.TP
.BI pv\-settings " PV" " \fR...\fP"
.BR getPVSettings .
.TP
.B alarms \fR[\fIPV\fR ...]
.BR getLastAlarmsData .
.TP
.B alarm\-checks
.BR getAlarmsCheck .
.TP
.B console \fR[\fB\-\-lcount\fR \fIN\fR]
.B GetConsoleMsgs
(LID 260).
In watch mode the returned count becomes the next
.IR lcount .
.TP
.B messages \fR[\fB\-\-history\fR]
.B getSystemMessages
(LID 200).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Connection (all commands)
.TP
.BI \-\-instance " NAME"
Profile under
.BR otsdaq.instances .
Default:
.BR MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_OTSDAQ_INSTANCE ,
then
.BR otsdaq.default_instance .
Without a profile, a gateway URL from an option, the environment or the
top-level
.B otsdaq
block is required.
.TP
.BI \-\-gateway\-url " ORIGIN"
.TP
.BI \-\-slow\-controls\-url " ORIGIN"
.TP
.BI \-\-tfm\-url " ORIGIN"
Override the origins.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Per request; default 10; must be positive.
.TP
.BR \-\-verify\-tls ", " \-\-insecure
Enable or disable certificate verification.
The shipped default is disabled, and every invocation prints
.B "warning: TLS certificate verification is disabled"
on stderr.
A configured CA bundle forces verification on, even with
.BR \-\-insecure .
.TP
.BI \-\-ca\-bundle " FILE"
CA bundle; must exist; enables verification.
.SS Read commands
.TP
.B \-\-json
One JSON object per sample:
.BR "{\(dqinstance\(dq, \(dqcommand\(dq, \(dqtimestamp\(dq, \(dqdata\(dq}" .
With
.BR \-\-watch ,
newline-delimited.
.TP
.B \-\-watch
Repeat until Ctrl-C or
.BR \-\-count .
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " SECONDS"
Default 2; must be positive.
.TP
.BI \-\-count " N"
Stop after
.I N
samples; requires
.BR \-\-watch .
.SS raw
.TP
.BI \-\-service " NAME"
.BR gateway ,
.BR console ,
.BR config ,
.BR slow\-controls ,
.B tfm
or
.BR macro ;
selects both LID and origin.
Default
.BR gateway .
.TP
.BI \-\-lid " N"
Explicit LID.
The origin follows
.B \-\-service
when given, otherwise the LID: 282 Slow Controls, 302 TFM, anything else the
gateway.
.TP
.BR \-\-handler " request|state\-machine"
Default
.BR request .
.TP
.BI \-\-query " KEY=VALUE"
URL query parameter; repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-form " KEY=VALUE"
Form body field; repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-xml
Print the response XML exactly instead of normalized JSON.
.SH FILES
The config file of
.BR mu2edaq\-tools (1),
section
.BR otsdaq :
.PP
.RS
.nf
otsdaq:
  default_instance: crv
  timeout: 10.0
  verify_tls: false
  ca_bundle: null
  instances:
    crv:
      gateway_url: https://localhost:3075
      slow_controls_url: https://localhost:3076   # optional
      tfm_url: https://localhost:3047             # optional
      cookie_file: ~/.config/mu2edaq/crv\-cookie   # optional, path only
.fi
.RE
.PP
Top-level
.B otsdaq
keys are defaults for every profile; profile keys override them;
environment variables override both; options override everything.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_OTSDAQ_INSTANCE ", " _GATEWAY_URL ", " _SLOW_CONTROLS_URL ", " _TFM_URL ", " _TIMEOUT ", " _VERIFY_TLS ", " _CA_BUNDLE ", " _COOKIE_FILE
Override the selected profile.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_OTSDAQ_COOKIE
CookieCode value.
When set, the cookie file is not read.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
The CookieCode comes from
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_OTSDAQ_COOKIE
or from the profile's
.BR cookie_file .
On POSIX the file must have no group or other permission bits (for example
0600 or 0400), or every command fails.
The file is read for every command, although only requests to LID 281 carry
it, as the form field
.BR CookieCode ;
no typed read uses LID 281.
.B raw \-\-lid 281
with
.B \-\-service tfm
or
.B slow\-controls
sends it to that origin.
The value never appears in an error message or in
.BR "mu2edaq\-tools config" .
A
.B \-\-form CookieCode=...
supplied by hand is visible in the process list and shell history.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration, transport, HTTP, XML, embedded-JSON or otsdaq error.
.TP
.B 2
No read command, invalid option value, or malformed
.IR KEY=VALUE .
.TP
.B 130
Watch mode interrupted.
.SH BUGS
.B macros
splits each
.B FEMacros
value on
.B :
and expects no tooltip field.
The newer otsdaq\-mu2e web client
.RI ( UserWebGUI/js/Mu2eHardware.js )
splits the same value on
.B ;
and reads a tooltip after the permission field.
Which format the deployed otsdaq emits is not determined here; with the
semicolon format
.B macros
fails with a protocol error.
.B "raw getFEMacroList \-\-service macro \-\-xml"
shows the raw value.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq\-tools otsdaq state \-\-instance crv
mu2edaq\-tools otsdaq pv\-read Mu2e:TDAQ_crv:daq08DTC:Temperature \-\-json
mu2edaq\-tools otsdaq daq\-state \-\-watch \-\-count 5 \-\-json
mu2edaq\-tools otsdaq \-\-help
mu2edaq\-tools otsdaq raw getAppStatus \-\-service gateway \-\-xml
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-tools (1),
.BR mu2edaq_commandline_tools (3)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group.
